{"kind":"artifact","text":"Every MCP tool now advertises an outputSchema, and it deliberately promises almost nothing. Exact clean pushed head 284f9002139d0c5beb44c8696f414c7976bb1cc2 on request/mcp-output-schema; tree f3907cb3, checkout clean, origin matching, parent is current main ebdca9fa, verified at filing. Under planner's request 206708ca and my promise 9c20ee34.\n\nTHE SCHEMA IS {\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":true} ON ALL FOURTEEN TOOLS, and the restraint is the design rather than laziness. Declaring an outputSchema makes conformant clients validate structuredContent against it and reject what does not conform, so a wrong schema is strictly worse than none: none degrades to today's behaviour, a wrong one breaks a client that works. The request's caveat said this and it governed every decision here.\n\nNO KEY IS NAMED, because none could be proved present on every return path. Every resident-backed tool has a degraded local-fold fallback that returns a differently shaped value — status falls back to a digest, wait to digestWait, work and artifacts and inspect to statusview builders, whoami to BuildOrientation with degraded true and a different source — and submit conditionally adds degraded, warning and projected. A key proved on the resident path is not thereby present on the fallback. Naming one would have rejected responses that are correct today, which is the exact failure the caveat warns about, and I would rather ship a schema that admits everything and tighten it later against observed responses.\n\nWHY type object IS SAFE RATHER THAN ASSUMED SAFE. structuredContent is exactly the value dispatch returns, and every success path returns either a Go map — whoami, presence, the submit family, reassign_if_unclaimed, say and ack — or a statusview value struct: ActorStatus, WaitDelta, WorkPage, ArtifactPage, ItemInspection. Both encode as JSON objects. The failure path carries no structuredContent at all, so there is nothing there to validate.\n\nTHE ENVELOPE DISTINCTION WAS CONFIRMED ON THE WIRE, not inferred. The result's keys are _meta, content, isError, live_attention, resultType and structuredContent, so isError and live_attention are siblings of the payload rather than inside it. Scoping the schema to the envelope instead would have produced precisely the over-strict schema this change exists to avoid.\n\nTHE SCHEMA IS ATTACHED BY A LOOP over the definitions rather than repeated in each, so a tool added later cannot forget it. That is the difference between fixing fourteen cases and fixing the shape.\n\nONE CONDITION OF THE REQUEST IS NOT MET AND I AM NOT REPORTING IT AS MET. It asks to verify against a real client that structuredContent is now recognised. I did not achieve that. The only real client within reach is this session's adapter, which runs an older binary; exercising it would demonstrate the old behaviour, and rebuilding or restarting the running resident was outside this row.\n\nWHAT WAS VERIFIED INSTEAD, stated as exactly what it is. A binary built from this head, driven over stdio with a scripted JSON-RPC client against the real workroom, returned fourteen tools each carrying an object-typed outputSchema, all one distinct value; and tools/call whoami returned isError false with structuredContent a JSON object conforming to it. That proves the schemas are on the wire and that a real response satisfies them. It does not prove any client's interface now surfaces the payload, which is the thing hugh actually reported. The probe was read-only and the running resident was neither restarted nor rebuilt.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE. Skipping one tool in the attach loop fails TestStatelessDiscoverAndToolList by name, reporting the tool that declares no object outputSchema. Restored, and the test passes.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit, with exit codes captured directly rather than through a pipe. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok, zero failures, zero cached. npm test 132 pass, 0 fail. gofmt -l . empty; go build, go vet and git diff --check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"284f9002139d0c5beb44c8696f414c7976bb1cc2","dead_basis_override":"true","path":"cmd/gitseq-mcp"}}